# Files are checked out EXACTLY as stored, with no line-ending translation.
#
# This matters here. SHA256SUMS.txt commits to the hash of every tracked file, and those
# hashes were computed on the stored (LF) bytes. Marking text files as `text` — as this
# file previously did — makes git rewrite LF to CRLF when checking out on Windows, so the
# working copy no longer matches the manifest and 132 of 166 files fail verification for
# no reason other than the platform someone cloned on. `-text` prevents that, so the
# checksums verify identically on Linux, macOS and Windows.
* -text

# Binary formats: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.docx binary
